From d3002e06fd3b816df08ce90864c1e5a0a71ab108 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:08:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Play refits the resident scene each step instead of
 rebuilding it

FrontierRuntime published one deforming physics step with the load-time path:
RefreshGeometry + BuildBottomLevel + UploadScene. UploadScene waits for the
device to go idle, reallocates and re-uploads every scene extent, rebuilds the
emitter cache, reconstructs the hardware BLAS and TLAS, rewrites the descriptor
sets and re-examines the distance atlas. ProjectDriveInterchange bumps
GeometryRevision every tick because the XPBD tyres genuinely deform, so this
ran at 240 Hz.

But GeometrySequence::Advance refuses any step that changes a vertex count, an
index count or an index value, and it resets a deformed subject's World to
identity so the positions already carry the pose. The resident structures stay
valid across the step and only need refitting. The rebuild was never necessary.

The Play loop now takes SwapchainExchange::RefreshDeformation when
TraversalIndex::IsRefittable and RefitBottomLevel succeed, and falls back to
BuildBottomLevel + UploadScene only when the refit or the publish refuses -
which is to say only when the topology really moved. Both arms are counted and
printed when the transport stops:

  [Playback] transport stopped: refit steps N, rebuild steps 0,
             worst traversal refit X ms, UploadScene calls 1,
             distance-field bakes 1

RefreshDeformation is four no-reallocation stages:
  1 VisibilityExchange::RefreshDeformation - vertices, cluster bounds and flat
    triangles memcpy'd into the extents UploadScene already allocated
  2 RefreshTraversal - the refitted CWBVH blobs, and the flat triangles again,
    now through UploadTrianglesInPlace so no vkDeviceWaitIdle and no
    descriptor rewrite
  3 RefreshInstances - instance rows, atlas placements, RT placement rows
  4 RayQueryExchange::RefreshVertices - stages the deformed vertices for a
    MODE_UPDATE build of the bottom levels inside the frame command buffer

RayQueryExchange gains ALLOW_UPDATE_BIT on the bottom-level builds, retained
geometry and range records, a persistent host mapping of the vertex extent, and
a MODE_UPDATE arm in RecordRefit. A purely rigid step leaves VerticesPending
clear and pays only the TLAS refit it always paid.

The distance atlas was already bake-once - Matches() is a count comparison and
a deformation cannot move a count - but the bake trigger is now logged with its
cost, so an editor-triggered rebuild is visible.

DistanceAtlasChecks gains two checks, both passing: deforming vertices never
re-bakes the atlas, and the baked field survives a playback deformation.
